<section class="section">
  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p class="section-intro">
    Hand <code>buildSchema</code> a Drizzle database instance and it returns a
    <code>GraphQLSchema</code> with list and single-row queries and create, update
    and delete mutations for every table. It works with PostgreSQL, MySQL and
    SQLite. Serve the schema as is with any GraphQL server, or take the generated
    types, inputs and resolvers from <code>entities</code> and build your own.
  </p>

  <ul class="card-grid">
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Filters and pagination</h3>
        <p>Every list query takes typed <code>where</code>, <code>orderBy</code>, <code>limit</code> and <code>offset</code> arguments, with cursor pagination, aggregates and group-by alongside.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Relations without N+1</h3>
        <p>Nested relations load in one round-trip through Drizzle's relational queries, and the standalone relation resolvers batch sibling loads into a single query.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
    <li>
      <article class="card">
        <h3>Configurable writes</h3>
        <p>Mutations cover upserts, nested writes and atomic column updates, and options turn operations off, exclude tables or columns, scope rows per request and run write hooks.</p>
      </article>
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="section" id="start">
  <h2>Get started</h2>
  <div class="prose">
    <pre class="code"><code>npm i @vantreeseba/drizzle-graphql</code></pre>
    <p><code>drizzle-orm</code>, <code>graphql</code> and <code>graphql-scalars</code> are peer dependencies. Then pass in your Drizzle instance:</p>
    <pre class="code"><code>import { buildSchema } from '@vantreeseba/drizzle-graphql';
import { db } from './database'; // your drizzle instance

const { schema, entities } = buildSchema(db);</code></pre>
  </div>

  <p class="readme-link">
    Full documentation lives in the project README:
    <a href="{{ site.repo }}#readme" rel="noopener">{{ site.repo }}</a>
  </p>
</section>
